@prefix backlog: <http://example.org/backlog#> .
@prefix ex:      <http://example.org/sen0414-ch1011simp-lineage#> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<http://example.org/sen0414-ch1011simp-lineage> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Urgent narrow lineage: SEN0414 chapters 10 and 11, one code, one environment"@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.2.0" ; owl:versionIRI <http://example.org/sen0414-ch1011simp-lineage/1.2.0> ; dcterms:identifier "sen0414_ch1011simp_lineage" ;
    rdfs:comment """1.2.0 (2026-11-20): Scope change only (one stage per version). A new gap becomes a scope item first, through the change route (request, impact assessment, owner-decided scope change), never as ad hoc work. The Owner asked at 17:52 Istanbul that the corrections and enhancements be adapted so that other chapters and other courses can apply them."""@en .

ex:CR11_Reuse a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "Make the code corrections applicable to other chapters and other courses"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope11 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Owner's instruction of 2026-11-20 17:52 Istanbul (content, not a verbatim quotation): add an adaptation of these corrections and enhancements so that they apply to other chapters and even other courses." ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .

ex:IA11_Reuse a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What reuse across chapters and courses needs, with the facts measured before it is planned"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR11_Reuse ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage11 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "MEASURED FACTS (2026-11-20, read-only): the repository holds 43 chapter-code manifests, all with the same example shape (order, id, name, slide, concepts, code, expected; some add recorded), so one shared source format and one generic check can serve every chapter without changing their shape. Chapters 10 and 11 show three faults that any chapter can have: code that is not the book's (7 and 8 percent of lines match), code split over boxes (all 37 code slides), slide and page examples that differ (5 of 37). IMPACT: a generic check and a generic source-to-slide-and-page step are built once inside this lineage and proven on chapters 10 and 11; they carry no chapter-specific text. Other chapters and other courses are NOT converted here; they adopt the method in their own lineages. Course-neutral wording goes in a written method guide in the course meta-model's own place, handed over through that repository's standard handover folder only if the Owner asks." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Cost named: two more areas, a reusable tool set and a method guide; the two chapters stay the only chapters converted." .

ex:Area11_Reuse a backlog:ScopeArea ; rdfs:label "Reusable method and tools for other chapters and courses"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage11 .
ex:Del11_Check a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "Generic code check: slide, page and source equal, one box per code, every example runs"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage11 ; backlog:deliverableForArea ex:Area11_Reuse .
ex:Del11_Make a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "Generic step that makes slide code, page example and Slide code tab from one source"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage11 ; backlog:deliverableForArea ex:Area11_Reuse .
ex:Del11_Guide a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "Course-neutral method guide: how to take a book's code into slide and page"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage11 ; backlog:deliverableForArea ex:Area11_Reuse .
ex:Excl11_OtherChapterConversion a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "Converting any chapter other than 10 and 11, or any other course's material"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage11 ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "They adopt the method in their own narrow lineages; here it is only proven on chapters 10 and 11." .

ex:SC11_Reuse a backlog:ScopeChange ;
    rdfs:label "Scope grown by a reusable method, its tools and a course-neutral guide"@en ;
    backlog:fulfillsRequest ex:CR11_Reuse ; backlog:changesScope ex:Scope11 ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner ;
    backlog:admitsItem ex:Area11_Reuse, ex:Del11_Check, ex:Del11_Make, ex:Del11_Guide ;
    backlog:hasScopeChangeRationale "Owner's instruction of 2026-11-20 17:52 Istanbul. The boundary moves outward by one area and three deliverables, and the exclusion of other chapters stays: reuse means the method is ready for them, not that they are converted. Cost named: more tooling work in this urgent lineage, so the chapter 10 and 11 pages come first and the reusable tools are made from what those two chapters need." .
ex:Scope11 backlog:coversArea ex:Area11_Reuse ; backlog:hasScopeDeliverable ex:Del11_Check, ex:Del11_Make, ex:Del11_Guide ; backlog:hasScopeExclusion ex:Excl11_OtherChapterConversion .
